name: sim.setJointTargetVelocity
description: Sets the target linear/angular velocity of a non-spherical joint. When in kinematic mode, the joint moves according to a motion profile that respects maximum acceleration and jerk values. In dynamic and velocity control mode, the controller is instructed about the desired velocity
luaSynopsis: sim.setJointTargetVelocity(int objectHandle, float targetVelocity, float[] motionParams = [])
pythonSynopsis: sim.setJointTargetVelocity(int objectHandle, float targetVelocity, float[] motionParams = {})
inputs:
1. objectHandle: handle of the joint object
2. targetVelocity: target velocity of the joint
3. motionParams: when the joint is in kinematic mode: the maximum allowed acceleration and jerk. When in dynamic mode with motion profile control enabled: the maximum allowed acceleration and jerk. Can be None/nil for default values. See also the maxVelAccelJerk property
outputs:
